  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"5.8.9\"\n\npackage:\n  name: podman\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/containers/podman/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 16959c84bf0df1ebf15aa0e5d2b0f6bcaeb8d0852ed4d44c5c344e44831cc6e5\n  target_directory: src/github.com/containers/podman\n  patches:\n    # The Windows remote client does not use local container configuration.\n    - if: not win\n      then: 0002-relative-paths-for-system-config-and-binaries.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('go-cgo') }}\n        - pkg-config\n      else:\n        - ${{ compiler('go') }}\n    - go-licenses\n    - if: not win\n      then:\n        - go-md2man\n        - make\n    - if: osx\n      then: grep\n  host:\n    - if: not win\n      then: containers-common\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - btrfs-progs\n        # Header and pkg-config files for libglib are in glib.\n        - glib\n        - libglib\n        - gpgme\n        - libassuan\n        - libgpg-error\n        - libseccomp\n        - libsqlite\n        # Enables healthcheck timers and journald, gated on a running systemd.\n        # A user session is needed for healthchecks unless DISABLE_HC_SYSTEMD=true.\n        - libsystemd\n  run:\n    - if: not win\n      then: containers-common\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - conmon >=2.0.30\n        - cni-plugins\n        - runc\n        - netavark\n        - slirp4netns\n    # These packages are not yet available for the other Linux architectures.\n    - if: linux and x86_64\n      then:\n        - aardvark-dns\n        - passt\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - if: win\n        then: run_test.bat\n        else: run_test.sh\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        # Avoid adding system utilities to the runtime environment.\n        - if: linux\n          then: util-linux\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://podman.io/\n  repository: https://github.com/containers/podman\n  documentation: https://docs.podman.io/en/latest/\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - src/github.com/containers/podman/LICENSE\n    - license-files/\n  summary: 'Podman: A tool for managing OCI containers and pods.'\n  description: >\n    Podman (the POD MANager) is a tool for managing containers and images, volumes mounted into those containers, and pods made from groups of containers. Podman is based on libpod, a library for container lifecycle management that is also contained in this repository. The libpod library provides APIs for managing containers,\n    pods, container images, and volumes.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - mbargull\n    - dhirschfeld\n    - manics\n    - xhochy\n",
